    "durationMs": 267656,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Stack**: Laravel 11.57.1 on PHP 8.3, Eloquent over the provided MySQL (`bench` DB), with all `DB_*` settings read from the environment (`.env` DB lines are commented out, so env vars are the sole source).\n\n**Implementation**:\n- `links` migration: unique `code` (20 chars), `url` text, `clicks` counter — persistent across restarts.\n- `LinkController`: `store` (validates absolute http/https URL with host, optional 4–20 char `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` code, generates unique 8-char codes with collision retry, `409` on duplicate custom code), `show`, `redirect` (atomic SQL `increment`, exact-once, `302` with Location), `index` (ascending by id, `items`/`total`).\n- Routes in `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}` with no `/api` prefix.\n- `ForceJsonResponse` middleware plus exception renderers so every error is JSON with an `error` field: `422` (malformed JSON, bad/missing url or code), `404`, `409`.\n- `start.sh`: `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` — I confirmed in the ServeCommand source that without `--no-reload`, env vars outside a passthrough list would be dropped.\n- README gained a \"Running the server\" section plus an API table.\n\n**Verification**: a 33-assertion test script covering every requirement passed 0 failures; a full restart confirmed clicks/data persist (5 clicks survived); a cold-start smoke test via `sh start.sh` worked end to end. The server is stopped, port 8000 is free, and the database was reset to pristine empty state for the graded run."
  }
